Task 1:
///Lab: Remote code execution via web shell upload///

Open the site in burp, log in, and upload an avatar. Look at the requests in burp. Notice that after you uploaded your avatar pic when you get back to your account page, the site loads in your uploaded avatar.
In the source code it looks like this:
                           <p>
                            <img src="/files/avatars/avatar.jpg" class=avatar>
                            </p>
This means the site saves your pic into the /file/avatars/ directory and then it directly loads in. We can use this. Create a php file ("To solve the lab, upload a basic PHP web shell")
and copy this into the php file: 
<?php echo file_get_contents('/home/carlos/secret'); ?>
Save it as xyz.php (i named it as secret.php) and upload this php file as your avatar. After you uploaded it you will see a GET /files/avatars/secret.php HTTP/2 request.
In the response you will see what the secret file contains. Submit it, and the lab is solved.

