Task 3:
///Lab: Web shell upload via path traversal///

Do the same in task 1. As you can see the site allowed you to upload the php file, but instead of executing the file it just returned the contents of the PHP file.
To bypass this: find the POST /my-account/avatar request and at the middle of the request you will find this line:
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="avatar"; filename="secret.php"
Since its a path traversal lab change the filename value to ../secret.php. In the response: The file avatars/secret.php has been uploaded. This indicates us, that the server is not allowing us to use the '/'
character, so url encode it to %2f:..%2fexploit.php. The response is: The file avatars/../exploit.php has been uploaded.
Which is good. If you go back to http history you will find a GET /files/avatars/..%2fsecret.php HTTP/2 request, where is got 404 not found. So send this to repeater, modify the request:
GET /files/avatars/../secret.php HTTP/2
And you will get the secret.

